(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m3"] = E["hr-m3"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-3-2"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Behavioural questions","tr":"Davranışsal sorular","fa":"سؤال‌های رفتاری"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can ask behavioural questions about past experience and follow up for real evidence.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda geçmiş deneyimle ilgili davranışsal sorular sorabilecek, takip sorularıyla gerçek kanıta ulaşabileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی درباره‌ی تجربه‌های گذشته سؤال رفتاری بپرسی و با سؤال تکمیلی به شواهد واقعی برسی."},"hook":{"en":"Ask for one real event, not opinions. Anyone can say \"I'm good under pressure\"; you need what they actually did. Deniz's first answer was a script about 'we'. One follow-up question got the real story.","tr":"Görüş değil, tek bir gerçek olay iste. \"Baskı altında iyiyim\" demek kolaydır; sana adayın gerçekte ne yaptığı lazım. Deniz'in ilk cevabı 'biz' hakkında ezber bir metindi. Tek bir takip sorusu gerçek hikâyeyi ortaya çıkardı.","fa":"نظر نخواه، یک اتفاق واقعی را بخواه. هر کسی می‌تواند بگوید «زیر فشار خوب کار می‌کنم»؛ تو باید بدانی واقعاً چه کرده است. جواب اول دنیز یک متن حفظی درباره‌ی «ما» بود. یک سؤال پیگیری، ماجرای واقعی را بیرون کشید."},"before":{"en":"Write fair notes on a candidate’s answer: the situation, what they did, the result and one line of evaluation.","tr":"Bir adayın cevabı hakkında adil notlar yaz: durum, yaptıkları, sonuç ve tek satırlık bir değerlendirme.","fa":"درباره‌ی جواب یک داوطلب یادداشت منصفانه بنویس: موقعیت، کاری که کرد، نتیجه و یک خط ارزیابی."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"5"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Ask for one real event","tr":"Tek bir gerçek olay iste","fa":"یک اتفاق واقعی را بخواه"},"body":{"en":"A general question gets a practised answer. So ask for one real moment, then follow up for the action and the result.","tr":"Genel bir soru ezberlenmiş bir cevap getirir. Bu yüzden tek bir gerçek anı sor, sonra yapılan işi ve sonucu sormaya devam et.","fa":"سؤال کلی جواب حفظ‌شده می‌گیرد. پس یک لحظه‌ی واقعی را بپرس و بعد با سؤال تکمیلی کاری را که کرده و نتیجه‌اش را بپرس."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Questions about past experience","tr":"Geçmiş deneyim soruları","fa":"سؤال درباره‌ی تجربه‌ی گذشته"},"steps":[{"en":"One real, finished moment: past simple.","tr":"Gerçek, bitmiş tek bir an: past simple.","fa":"برای یک لحظه‌ی واقعی و تمام‌شده، گذشته‌ی ساده می‌آید.","ex":"Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict."},{"en":"Ask for actions: What exactly did you do?","tr":"Eylemleri sor: What exactly did you do?","fa":"درباره‌ی کارهایش بپرس: ⁨What exactly did you do?⁩","ex":"What exactly did you do?"},{"en":"After a polite opener: statement order, no did.","tr":"Kibar bir girişten sonra: düz cümle sırası, did yok.","fa":"بعد از شروع مؤدبانه، ترتیب خبری می‌آید، بدون did.","ex":"Can you tell me what you did next?"},{"en":"Close with the result.","tr":"Sonuçla bitir.","fa":"با نتیجه تمامش کن.","ex":"What was the outcome?"}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Purpose","Pattern"],"tr":["Amaç","Kalıp"],"fa":["هدف","الگو"]},"rows":[["Open the story","Tell me about a time when you + past simple"],["Get the action","What exactly did you do?"],["Get the result","What was the result?"],["Polite version","Can you tell me what you did / why you decided ...?"]]},"tip":{"en":"Persian bargu che kar kardi and Turkish ne yaptığını anlat both keep the past without a helper, so 'did' slips into indirect questions. After the opener, English drops did.","tr":"Türkçede 'Bir sonraki adımda ne yaptığını anlatır mısın?' derken soru yapısı kurulmaz. İngilizcede de giriş kalıbından sonra did düşer: Can you tell me what you did next?","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «می‌شود بگویی بعدش چه کار کردی؟» و ساختار سؤالی نمی‌سازیم. در انگلیسی هم بعد از عبارت شروع did حذف می‌شود: «⁨Can you tell me what you did next?⁩»"},"wrong":"Could you tell me what did you do?","right":"Could you tell me what you did?"},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"Tell me about a time when...","meaning":{"en":"The standard opener for a behavioural question.","tr":"Davranışsal sorunun standart girişi.","fa":"شروع استاندارد سؤال رفتاری."}},{"phrase":"What exactly did you do?","meaning":{"en":"Moves from the team to the person.","tr":"Takımdan kişiye geçer.","fa":"از کار تیم به کار خود فرد می‌رسد."}},{"phrase":"What was the outcome?","meaning":{"en":"Asks for the result, the R in STAR.","tr":"Sonucu sorar, STAR'daki R.","fa":"نتیجه را می‌پرسد؛ همان R در STAR."}},{"phrase":"evidence","meaning":{"en":"Facts that show something is true.","tr":"kanıt.","fa":"شواهد؛ مدرک و دلیل"}},{"phrase":"under pressure","meaning":{"en":"When there is stress, little time or high stakes.","tr":"baskı altında.","fa":"تحت فشار (وقتی استرس زیاد، وقت کم یا ریسک بالاست)"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"\"We\" can be modesty","tr":"\"We\" alçakgönüllülük olabilir","fa":"«we» گاهی از سر فروتنی است"},"body":{"en":"In many UK and US interviews, \"I\" is expected when you describe your own work, and too much \"we\" can hide what you did. Candidates from cultures where talking about yourself feels like boasting often say \"we\" out of modesty. A good interviewer knows this and simply asks again, kindly.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan mülakatında kendi işini anlatırken \"ben\" demen beklenir; fazla \"biz\" ne yaptığını gizleyebilir. Kendinden bahsetmenin övünmek gibi algılandığı kültürlerden gelen adaylar alçakgönüllülükten \"biz\" der. İyi bir mülakatçı bunu bilir ve nazikçe yeniden sorar.","fa":"در بسیاری از مصاحبه‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، انتظار دارند وقتی از کار خودت حرف می‌زنی بگویی «من»؛ زیاد گفتن «ما» سهم خودت را پنهان می‌کند. متقاضیانی که در فرهنگی بزرگ شده‌اند که حرف زدن از خود را خودستایی می‌داند، از سر فروتنی «ما» می‌گویند؛ این برای بسیاری از ما ایرانی‌ها هم آشناست. مصاحبه‌گر خوب این را می‌داند و فقط با مهربانی دوباره می‌پرسد."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از سؤال کلی تا اتفاق واقعی"},"text":"Facts: You want to know how the person handled a plan that went wrong.","item":"Are you good under pressure?","why":{"en":"Weak: easy to fake. Strong: it asks for a real event.","tr":"Zayıf: uydurması kolay. Güçlü: gerçek bir olay istiyor.","fa":"به نسخه‌ی اول راحت می‌شود جواب ساختگی داد. نسخه‌ی دوم یک اتفاق واقعی می‌خواهد."},"answer":"Tell me about a time when a plan went wrong. What exactly did you do?","cut":["Are you good under pressure?"],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap the question that gets a practised answer, not a real event.","tr":"Gerçek bir olay değil, ezber bir cevap getiren soruya dokun.","fa":"روی سؤالی بزن که جواب حفظ‌شده می‌گیرد، نه یک اتفاق واقعی."}},"quick":{"prompt":"A candidate keeps saying \"we did...\" about their own project. What does a good interviewer do?","options":["Kindly ask: \"And what did you do yourself?\"","Mark it down as weak evidence","Move on to the next question"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Ask again, kindly: many candidates say we out of modesty. The follow-up gets the evidence without judging them.","tr":"Nazikçe yeniden sor: Birçok aday alçakgönüllülükten we der. Takip sorusu onları yargılamadan kanıtı ortaya çıkarır.","fa":"دوباره و با مهربانی بپرس: خیلی از داوطلب‌ها از روی فروتنی ⁨we⁩ می‌گویند. سؤال پیگیری بدون قضاوت کردنشان شواهد را بیرون می‌کشد."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Cover the opener. If what is left sounds like a normal sentence ('what you did next'), it is right. Result of this lesson: you can get real evidence. You also have fair notes on an answer.","tr":"Giriş kalıbını kapat. Geriye kalan normal bir cümle gibi duruyorsa ('what you did next'), doğrudur. Bu dersin sonucu: gerçek kanıt toplayabilirsin ve elinde bir cevapla ilgili adil notlar olur.","fa":"عبارت شروع را بپوشان. اگر چیزی که می‌ماند مثل یک جمله‌ی عادی است («what you did next»)، درست است. حالا می‌توانی مدرک واقعی بگیری. یادداشت‌های منصفانه درباره‌ی یک جواب هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Past perfect in follow-up questions","tr":"Takip sorularında past perfect","fa":"ماضی بعید در سؤال‌های پیگیری"},"steps":[{"en":"The earlier of two past actions: had + past participle.","tr":"İki geçmiş eylemden önce olanı: had + past participle.","fa":"برای کاری که از دو کار گذشته قدیمی‌تر است، had و اسم مفعول می‌آید.","ex":"When I arrived, the truck had already left."},{"en":"Question: had + subject + past participle.","tr":"Soru: had + özne + past participle.","fa":"در سؤال، اول had می‌آید، بعد فاعل و بعد اسم مفعول.","ex":"What had you already tried?"},{"en":"In a past story, not has: had.","tr":"Geçmişteki bir hikâyede has değil, had.","fa":"در داستانی که در گذشته است، had بیاور، نه has.","ex":"Deniz had already called two drivers."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Use","Example"],"tr":["Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["Earlier past action","By the time his manager called back, he had already called two drivers."],["Follow-up question","What had you already tried before you asked for help?"],["Checking the order","Had the client complained before you called?"]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: add one follow-up question in the past perfect to your speaking task (for example \"What had you already tried before...?\").","tr":"B2 yolu: konuşma görevine past perfect ile bir takip sorusu ekle (örneğin \"What had you already tried before...?\").","fa":"مسیر B2: یک سؤال تکمیلی با ماضی بعید به تمرین گفتاری‌ات اضافه کن (مثلاً «⁨What had you already tried before...?⁩»)."}},"source":{"en":"Informed by SHRM guidance on behavioural interview questions.","tr":"SHRM’nin davranışsal mülakat soruları rehberinden yararlanır.","fa":"با استفاده از راهنمای SHRM درباره‌ی سؤال‌های رفتاری مصاحبه."}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","title":"Questions about past experience","titleTr":"Geçmiş deneyim soruları","exp":{"en":"A behavioural question asks about one real, finished moment, so the story is in the past simple: \"Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict.\" Not \"have solved\": the question points to one specific time, and specific finished times take the past simple. The second trap is the polite form. Once you start with \"Can you tell me...\" or \"Could you explain...\", the rest of the sentence goes back to normal statement order: \"Can you tell me what you did next?\", never \"what did you do next?\". The polite opener has already done the asking. Quick test: cover the opener. If what is left sounds like a normal sentence (\"what you did next\"), it's right.","tr":"Davranışsal bir soru gerçek ve bitmiş tek bir anı sorar, bu yüzden hikâye past simple ile anlatılır: \"Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict.\" \"Have solved\" değil, çünkü soru belirli tek bir zamanı gösterir. İkinci tuzak nazik soru kalıbıdır. Türkçede soru zaten fiilin içindedir (\"ne yaptığını anlatır mısın?\") ve kelime sırası değişmez. İngilizcede ise \"Can you tell me...\" ile başladıktan sonra cümlenin geri kalanı düz cümle sırasına döner: \"Can you tell me what you did next?\", asla \"what did you do next?\" değil. Kısa test: baştaki kalıbı kapat; kalan kısım normal bir cümle gibi okunuyorsa (\"what you did next\") doğrudur.","fa":"سؤال رفتاری (behavioural question) درباره‌ی یک موقعیت واقعی و تمام‌شده است؛ پس ماجرا با گذشته‌ی ساده تعریف می‌شود: «⁨Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict.⁩» اینجا have solved درست نیست، چون سؤال به یک بارِ مشخص در گذشته اشاره دارد و برای زمانِ مشخص و تمام‌شده گذشته‌ی ساده می‌آید. تله‌ی دوم، شکل مؤدبانه‌ی سؤال است. در فارسی ترتیب کلمه‌ها در سؤال عوض نمی‌شود («می‌شود بگویید بعدش چه کردید؟»)، اما در انگلیسی وقتی با «⁨Can you tell me...⁩» یا «⁨Could you explain...⁩» شروع می‌کنی، بقیه‌ی جمله به ترتیب جمله‌ی خبری برمی‌گردد: «⁨Can you tell me what you did next?⁩»، نه «⁨what did you do next?⁩». کار پرسیدن را همان عبارت مؤدبانه‌ی اول انجام داده است. یک آزمون ساده: عبارت شروع را با دست بپوشان؛ اگر باقی‌مانده مثل یک جمله‌ی معمولی بود («what you did next»)، جمله درست است."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Purpose","Pattern"],"tr":["Amaç","Kalıp"],"fa":["هدف","الگو"]},"rows":[["Open the story","Tell me about a time when you + past simple"],["Get the action","What exactly did you do?"],["Get the result","What was the result?"],["Polite version","Can you tell me what you did / why you decided ...?"]]},"wrong":"Tell me about a time when you have solved a conflict.","right":"Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict.","blank":{"sentence":"Tell me about a time when you ___ a difficult customer.","word":"handled","distractors":["handle","are handling"]},"wrong2":"Can you tell me what did you do next?","right2":"Can you tell me what you did next?","blank2":{"sentence":"Could you tell me ___ the team?","word":"why you left","distractors":["why did you leave","why left you"]},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"Deniz's first answer was a script about 'we'. One follow-up question got the real story.","tr":"Deniz'in ilk cevabı 'biz' hakkında ezber bir metindi. Tek bir takip sorusu gerçek hikâyeyi ortaya çıkardı.","fa":"جواب اول دنیز یک متن حفظی درباره‌ی «ما» بود. یک سؤال پیگیری، ماجرای واقعی را بیرون کشید."},"tryWhy":{"en":"why you left: after 'Could you tell me' the rest is a normal statement, with no did.","tr":"why you left: 'Could you tell me'den sonrası düz cümledir, did gelmez.","fa":"جواب why you left است: بعد از Could you tell me بقیه‌ی جمله خبری عادی است و did نمی‌آید."},"rule":[{"en":"One real, finished moment: past simple.","tr":"Gerçek, bitmiş tek bir an: past simple.","fa":"برای یک لحظه‌ی واقعی و تمام‌شده، گذشته‌ی ساده می‌آید.","ex":"Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict."},{"en":"Ask for actions: What exactly did you do?","tr":"Eylemleri sor: What exactly did you do?","fa":"درباره‌ی کارهایش بپرس: ⁨What exactly did you do?⁩","ex":"What exactly did you do?"},{"en":"After a polite opener: statement order, no did.","tr":"Kibar bir girişten sonra: düz cümle sırası, did yok.","fa":"بعد از شروع مؤدبانه، ترتیب خبری می‌آید، بدون did.","ex":"Can you tell me what you did next?"},{"en":"Close with the result.","tr":"Sonuçla bitir.","fa":"با نتیجه تمامش کن.","ex":"What was the outcome?"}],"test":{"en":"Cover the opener. If what is left sounds like a normal sentence ('what you did next'), it is right.","tr":"Giriş kalıbını kapat. Geriye kalan normal bir cümle gibi duruyorsa ('what you did next'), doğrudur.","fa":"عبارت شروع را بپوشان. اگر چیزی که می‌ماند مثل یک جمله‌ی عادی است («what you did next»)، درست است."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian bargu che kar kardi and Turkish ne yaptığını anlat both keep the past without a helper, so 'did' slips into indirect questions. After the opener, English drops did.","tr":"Türkçede 'Bir sonraki adımda ne yaptığını anlatır mısın?' derken soru yapısı kurulmaz. İngilizcede de giriş kalıbından sonra did düşer: Can you tell me what you did next?","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «می‌شود بگویی بعدش چه کار کردی؟» و ساختار سؤالی نمی‌سازیم. در انگلیسی هم بعد از عبارت شروع did حذف می‌شود: «⁨Can you tell me what you did next?⁩»"}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["a time when you have","a time you have","a time when you've"],"fix":{"en":"One specific past time takes the past simple: 'Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict.'","tr":"Geçmişte belirli tek bir zaman past simple ister: 'Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict.'","fa":"یک زمان مشخص در گذشته، گذشته‌ی ساده می‌خواهد: «⁨Tell me about a time when you solved a conflict.⁩»"}},{"find":["tell me what did you","tell me why did you","tell me how did you","tell me where did you","explain what did you","explain why did you"],"fix":{"en":"After 'Can you tell me', use statement order: 'Can you tell me what you did next?'","tr":"'Can you tell me'den sonra düz cümle sırası kullan: 'Can you tell me what you did next?'","fa":"بعد از «Can you tell me» ترتیب خبری بیاور: «⁨Can you tell me what you did next?⁩»"}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","title":"Past perfect in follow-up questions","titleTr":"Takip sorularında past perfect","exp":{"en":"Strong follow-up questions find out what happened before the main action, because that shows judgement: \"What had you already tried before you called your manager?\" When two past actions are told out of order, the earlier one takes the past perfect (had + past participle): \"By the time his manager called back, Deniz had already called two drivers.\" In the question form, had moves before the subject and the verb stays a past participle: \"What had you tried?\", not \"What had you try?\" or \"What did you already tried?\". Do not use the present perfect with a finished past time: not \"he has already called\" when the story is in the past.","tr":"Güçlü takip soruları asıl eylemden önce ne olduğunu ortaya çıkarır, çünkü bu kişinin muhakemesini gösterir: \"What had you already tried before you called your manager?\" İki geçmiş olay sırasız anlatıldığında daha önce olan past perfect alır (had + past participle): \"By the time his manager called back, Deniz had already called two drivers.\" Türkçedeki \"-mişti\" yapısına benzer. Soru biçiminde had öznenin önüne geçer ve fiil past participle olarak kalır: \"What had you tried?\"; \"What had you try?\" ya da \"What did you already tried?\" değil. Hikâye geçmişteyse present perfect kullanma: \"he has already called\" değil.","fa":"سؤال‌های تکمیلیِ قوی روشن می‌کنند که پیش از اقدام اصلی چه اتفاقی افتاده بود، چون این قدرت قضاوت فرد را نشان می‌دهد: «⁨What had you already tried before you called your manager?⁩» وقتی دو کارِ گذشته را به ترتیب وقوع تعریف نمی‌کنی، کاری که زودتر اتفاق افتاده ماضی بعید (past perfect) می‌گیرد، یعنی had + اسم مفعول؛ درست مثل «زنگ زده بود» در فارسی: «⁨By the time his manager called back, Deniz had already called two drivers.⁩» در سؤال، had قبل از فاعل می‌آید و فعل همان اسم مفعول می‌ماند: «⁨What had you tried?⁩»، نه «⁨What had you try?⁩» و نه «⁨What did you already tried?⁩». وقتی ماجرا در گذشته است، از حال کامل استفاده نکن: «he has already called» در این داستان غلط است."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Use","Example"],"tr":["Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["Earlier past action","By the time his manager called back, he had already called two drivers."],["Follow-up question","What had you already tried before you asked for help?"],["Checking the order","Had the client complained before you called?"]]},"wrong":"When I arrived, the truck already left.","right":"When I arrived, the truck had already left.","blank":{"sentence":"By the time his manager called back, Deniz ___ two other drivers.","word":"had already called","distractors":["already calls","has already called"]},"wrong2":"What had you already try before you asked for help?","right2":"What had you already tried before you asked for help?","blank2":{"sentence":"What ___ you already tried before you asked for help?","word":"had","distractors":["did","have"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: add one follow-up question in the past perfect to your speaking task (for example \"What had you already tried before...?\").","tr":"B2 yolu: konuşma görevine past perfect ile bir takip sorusu ekle (örneğin \"What had you already tried before...?\").","fa":"مسیر B2: یک سؤال تکمیلی با ماضی بعید به تمرین گفتاری‌ات اضافه کن (مثلاً «⁨What had you already tried before...?⁩»)."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-3-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"When Deniz arrived, the customer ___.","options":["had already left","already leaves","has already left"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"had already left: the customer left before Deniz arrived, so past perfect. 'Already leaves' is the present, and 'has already left' links to now.","tr":"had already left: müşteri Deniz gelmeden önce ayrıldı, bu yüzden past perfect. 'Already leaves' şimdiki zamandır; 'has already left' şimdiye bağlar.","fa":"had already left درست است، چون مشتری قبل از رسیدن Deniz رفته بود و گذشته‌ی کامل لازم است. already leaves زمان حال است و has already left به الان ربط دارد."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"What had Deniz already done before he called his manager? That earlier step shows his judgement.","tr":"Deniz, müdürünü aramadan önce neler yapmıştı? O önceki adım onun muhakemesini gösterir.","fa":"دنیز پیش از اینکه به مدیرش زنگ بزند چه کارهایی کرده بود؟ همین قدم قبلی نشان می‌دهد چطور قضاوت می‌کند."},"tryWhy":{"en":"had: the question is about the earlier past, so had moves before you and the verb stays tried.","tr":"had: soru daha önceki geçmişle ilgili; had öznenin önüne geçer ve fiil tried olarak kalır.","fa":"جواب had است: سؤال درباره‌ی گذشته‌ی دورتر است؛ پس had پیش از you می‌آید و فعل tried می‌ماند."},"rule":[{"en":"The earlier of two past actions: had + past participle.","tr":"İki geçmiş eylemden önce olanı: had + past participle.","fa":"برای کاری که از دو کار گذشته قدیمی‌تر است، had و اسم مفعول می‌آید.","ex":"When I arrived, the truck had already left."},{"en":"Question: had + subject + past participle.","tr":"Soru: had + özne + past participle.","fa":"در سؤال، اول had می‌آید، بعد فاعل و بعد اسم مفعول.","ex":"What had you already tried?"},{"en":"In a past story, not has: had.","tr":"Geçmişteki bir hikâyede has değil, had.","fa":"در داستانی که در گذشته است، had بیاور، نه has.","ex":"Deniz had already called two drivers."}],"test":{"en":"Two past actions in one sentence? Ask which came first. That one gets had.","tr":"Bir cümlede iki geçmiş eylem mi var? Hangisinin önce olduğunu sor. had onu alır.","fa":"در یک جمله دو کار گذشته هست؟ بپرس کدام اول اتفاق افتاده. had مال همان است."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian zang zade bud and Turkish aramıştı both have a clear past perfect, so the meaning is familiar. The trap is the form: had + past participle (tried, called), never the base verb.","tr":"Türkçedeki '-mıştı' (aramıştı) bu anlamı zaten verir. Tuzak biçimdedir: had + past participle (tried, called), yalın fiil değil.","fa":"در فارسی ماضی بعید داریم («زنگ زده بود»)، پس معنا آشناست. تله در شکل فعل است: had و اسم مفعول (tried، called)، نه شکل ساده‌ی فعل."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["had you try","had you already try","did you already tried","had already call","had already try"],"fix":{"en":"Use had + past participle: 'What had you already tried?'","tr":"had + past participle kullan: 'What had you already tried?'","fa":"از had و اسم مفعول استفاده کن: «What had you already tried?»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Interview Evidence","tr":"Mülakatta Kanıt","fa":"شواهد در مصاحبه"},"cards":[{"word":"competency","sentence":"Teamwork is one of the five competencies for this role.","gap":"competencies","accept":["competencies","competency"],"meaning":{"en":"A skill or behaviour the job needs.","tr":"yetkinlik.","fa":"شایستگی (مهارت یا رفتاری که شغل لازم دارد)"}},{"word":"behavioural question","sentence":"Start each behavioural question with \"Tell me about a time\".","meaning":{"en":"A question about what someone really did in the past.","tr":"davranışsal soru.","fa":"سؤال رفتاری (درباره‌ی کاری که فرد واقعاً در گذشته انجام داده)"}},{"word":"follow-up question","sentence":"Her follow-up question showed he had not led the project.","meaning":{"en":"A second question that asks for more detail.","tr":"takip sorusu.","fa":"سؤال تکمیلی؛ سؤالی برای گرفتن جزئیات بیشتر"}},{"word":"evidence","sentence":"We need evidence, not opinions, in the interview notes.","meaning":{"en":"Facts that show something is true.","tr":"kanıt.","fa":"شواهد؛ مدرک و دلیل"}},{"word":"outcome","sentence":"What was the outcome of your decision?","meaning":{"en":"The final result of an action.","tr":"sonuç.","fa":"نتیجه؛ پیامد نهایی"}},{"word":"take ownership","sentence":"Good candidates take ownership of their mistakes.","meaning":{"en":"To accept that something is your responsibility.","tr":"sorumluluk almak, sahiplenmek.","fa":"مسئولیت چیزی را پذیرفتن"}},{"word":"under pressure","sentence":"How do you work under pressure?","meaning":{"en":"When there is stress, little time or high stakes.","tr":"baskı altında.","fa":"تحت فشار (وقتی استرس زیاد، وقت کم یا ریسک بالاست)"}},{"word":"stakeholder","sentence":"He kept every stakeholder updated during the move.","meaning":{"en":"A person affected by or interested in a project.","tr":"paydaş.","fa":"ذی‌نفع (کسی که از یک پروژه اثر می‌پذیرد یا به آن علاقه دارد)"}},{"word":"walk me through","sentence":"Walk me through what happened that day.","meaning":{"en":"Explain something step by step.","tr":"adım adım anlat.","fa":"قدم‌به‌قدم برایم توضیح بده"}},{"word":"red flag","sentence":"Blaming every past manager is a red flag.","meaning":{"en":"A warning sign that something may be wrong.","tr":"tehlike işareti.","fa":"زنگ خطر؛ نشانه‌ی هشدار"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","title":{"en":"The Perfect Answer","tr":"Mükemmel Cevap","fa":"جواب بی‌نقص"},"text":"Deniz arrived ten minutes early. He wore a new blue shirt and held his phone in both hands, like it might run away.\n\nLeyla smiled and opened her notes. \"Thanks for coming in, Deniz. Today I'm going to ask you about real situations from your past jobs. There are no trick questions. I just want to hear what you actually did.\"\n\n\"Of course,\" Deniz said.\n\n\"Tell me about a time when you had a problem with a delivery deadline.\"\n\nDeniz answered quickly. \"In my last company we always worked under pressure. We were a great team. We planned everything carefully and we never missed a deadline.\"\n\nIt was a nice answer. It was also empty. Leyla wrote one word in her notes: we.\n\n\"That sounds like a strong team,\" she said. \"Can you walk me through one specific delivery? What exactly did you do?\"\n\nDeniz stopped. For a second he looked at the window. Then he spoke more slowly.\n\n\"Last March, a truck broke down near Izmit with medicine for three hospitals. My manager was on holiday. I called two other drivers, I asked the warehouse to repack the boxes into a smaller van, and I phoned each hospital myself to give them a new time.\"\n\n\"And what was the outcome?\"\n\n\"Two hospitals got everything on time. One was four hours late.\" He paused. \"I told them the truth before they had to ask. They still work with us.\"\n\nLeyla stopped writing for a moment. That was the answer. Not perfect, but real: a situation, his actions, a result, and he took ownership of the late one.\n\nAfter he left, Omar called from Dubai. \"So? Is he good?\"\n\n\"His first answer was a script,\" Leyla said. \"His second answer was evidence.\"\n\nOn the bus home, Deniz kept replaying the moment he looked at the window. Had he said too much about the late hospital? He had no idea that it was the best thing he said all day.","vocab":[{"word":"trick question","en":"A question made to catch you out.","tr":"tuzak soru","fa":"سؤال انحرافی؛ سؤالی برای غافلگیر کردن"},{"word":"deadline","en":"The latest time something must be done.","tr":"son teslim tarihi","fa":"مهلت؛ ضرب‌الاجل"},{"word":"empty","en":"Here: without real content or detail.","tr":"içi boş","fa":"توخالی؛ بدون محتوا و جزئیات واقعی"},{"word":"specific","en":"Clear and exact, about one thing.","tr":"belirli, somut","fa":"مشخص؛ دقیق"},{"word":"break down","en":"To stop working (a machine or vehicle).","tr":"arıza yapmak, bozulmak","fa":"خراب شدن؛ از کار افتادن (ماشین یا وسیله)"},{"word":"repack","en":"To pack again in a different way.","tr":"yeniden paketlemek","fa":"دوباره بسته‌بندی کردن"},{"word":"script","en":"Here: words prepared and repeated, not real.","tr":"ezber metin","fa":"متن از پیش حفظ‌شده"},{"word":"replay","en":"To go over something again in your mind.","tr":"kafasında tekrar tekrar düşünmek","fa":"دوباره در ذهن مرور کردن"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why did Leyla write the word \"we\" in her notes?","options":["Deniz talked about the team, not his own actions","Deniz forgot the team's name","She wanted to hire the whole team"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Which follow-up question asks for the result?","options":["What was the outcome?","Can you walk me through it?","Thanks for coming in."],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Choose the correct polite question.","options":["Can you tell me what you did?","Can you tell me what did you do?","Can you tell me what you do did?"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"How did Deniz probably feel on the bus?","options":["Unsure, because he told her about the late delivery","Angry with Leyla","Sure that he had failed the test on purpose"],"correct":0}],"notice":{"en":"Deniz gives two answers to the same question. Listen for one small word that changes between them.","tr":"Deniz aynı soruya iki cevap veriyor. İkisi arasında değişen küçük bir kelimeye dikkat et.","fa":"دنیز به یک سؤال دو جواب می‌دهد. دنبال یک کلمه‌ی کوچک بگرد که بین این دو جواب عوض می‌شود."},"bridge":{"en":"'What exactly did you do?' turned 'we' into 'I'. Next: see how questions about the past are built.","tr":"'What exactly did you do?' sorusu 'biz'i 'ben'e çevirdi. Sırada: geçmişle ilgili soruların nasıl kurulduğunu gör.","fa":"«⁨What exactly did you do?⁩» «ما» را به «من» تبدیل کرد. قدم بعد: ببین سؤال‌های مربوط به گذشته چطور ساخته می‌شوند."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-3-2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","topic":{"en":"Asking Behavioural Questions","tr":"Davranışsal Sorular Sormak","fa":"پرسیدن سؤال‌های رفتاری"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of a great colleague. What did they once do that showed it?","tr":"Harika bir iş arkadaşını düşün. Bunu gösteren, bir zamanlar yaptığı şey neydi?","fa":"به یک همکار عالی فکر کن. چه کاری از او دیدی که این را نشان داد؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Ask the candidate about a time they missed a deadline.","tr":"Adaya bir son teslim tarihini kaçırdığı bir zamanı sor.","fa":"از متقاضی بخواه از دفعه‌ای تعریف کند که کاری را تا مهلتش تمام نکرد."},{"en":"Ask about a time they disagreed with a manager.","tr":"Bir yöneticiyle aynı fikirde olmadığı bir zamanı sor.","fa":"درباره‌ی یک بار بپرس که با مدیرش هم‌نظر نبود."},{"en":"Ask about a time they had to learn something new very fast.","tr":"Çok hızlı yeni bir şey öğrenmek zorunda kaldığı bir zamanı sor.","fa":"درباره‌ی یک بار بپرس که مجبور شد چیز تازه‌ای را خیلی سریع یاد بگیرد."},{"en":"Ask about a mistake they made at work.","tr":"İşte yaptığı bir hatayı sor.","fa":"درباره‌ی اشتباهی بپرس که در محل کار مرتکب شد."}],"followups":[{"en":"The answer you hear is all \"we\". Ask a follow-up that gets \"I\".","tr":"Duyduğun cevap hep \"biz\" diyor. \"Ben\" cevabı getirecek bir takip sorusu sor.","fa":"جوابی که می‌شنوی سراسر «ما» است. یک سؤال تکمیلی بپرس که «من» را بیرون بکشد."},{"en":"Now ask two past-experience questions you would really use at your company.","tr":"Şimdi şirketinde gerçekten kullanacağın, geçmiş deneyimle ilgili iki soru sor.","fa":"حالا دو سؤال درباره‌ی تجربه‌ی گذشته بپرس که واقعاً در شرکتت از آن‌ها استفاده می‌کنی."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"Tell me about a time when...","meaning":{"en":"The standard opener for a behavioural question.","tr":"Davranışsal sorunun standart girişi.","fa":"شروع استاندارد سؤال رفتاری."}},{"phrase":"What exactly did you do?","meaning":{"en":"Moves from the team to the person.","tr":"Takımdan kişiye geçer.","fa":"از کار تیم به کار خود فرد می‌رسد."}},{"phrase":"What was the outcome?","meaning":{"en":"Asks for the result, the R in STAR.","tr":"Sonucu sorar, STAR'daki R.","fa":"نتیجه را می‌پرسد؛ همان R در STAR."}}],"culture":{"en":"In many UK and US interviews, \"I\" is expected when you describe your own work, and too much \"we\" can hide what you did. Candidates from cultures where talking about yourself feels like boasting often say \"we\" out of modesty. A good interviewer knows this and simply asks again, kindly.","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan mülakatında kendi işini anlatırken \"ben\" demen beklenir; fazla \"biz\" ne yaptığını gizleyebilir. Kendinden bahsetmenin övünmek gibi algılandığı kültürlerden gelen adaylar alçakgönüllülükten \"biz\" der. İyi bir mülakatçı bunu bilir ve nazikçe yeniden sorar.","fa":"در بسیاری از مصاحبه‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، انتظار دارند وقتی از کار خودت حرف می‌زنی بگویی «من»؛ زیاد گفتن «ما» سهم خودت را پنهان می‌کند. متقاضیانی که در فرهنگی بزرگ شده‌اند که حرف زدن از خود را خودستایی می‌داند، از سر فروتنی «ما» می‌گویند؛ این برای بسیاری از ما ایرانی‌ها هم آشناست. مصاحبه‌گر خوب این را می‌داند و فقط با مهربانی دوباره می‌پرسد."},"model":"Tell me about a time when you missed a deadline. Thank you. You said the team planned everything. Can you walk me through one specific delivery? What exactly did you do? And what had you already tried before you called your manager? I see. What was the outcome? And looking back, what would you do differently? Thank you, that is really helpful.","selfCheck":[{"en":"My questions asked about one real moment in the past simple.","tr":"Sorularım past simple ile gerçek tek bir anı sordu.","fa":"سؤال‌هایم با گذشته‌ی ساده درباره‌ی یک لحظه‌ی واقعی بود."},{"en":"When I heard 'we', I asked 'What exactly did you do?'","tr":"'Biz' duyduğumda 'What exactly did you do?' diye sordum.","fa":"وقتی «ما» شنیدم، پرسیدم «⁨What exactly did you do?⁩»"},{"en":"I asked for the outcome.","tr":"Sonucu sordum.","fa":"نتیجه را پرسیدم."},{"en":"After 'Can you tell me', I used statement order.","tr":"'Can you tell me'den sonra düz cümle sırası kullandım.","fa":"بعد از «Can you tell me» ترتیب خبری را رعایت کردم."}]},"judge":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-j","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","type":"judge","parts":["Situation","Task","Action","Result"],"instruction":{"en":"Read each answer. Tap the STAR parts you can find. Then see which follow-up question would get the missing part.","tr":"Her cevabı oku. Bulabildiğin STAR parçalarına dokun. Sonra eksik parçayı hangi takip sorusunun getireceğini gör.","fa":"هر جواب را بخوان و بخش‌هایی از STAR را که در آن پیدا می‌کنی لمس کن. بعد ببین کدام سؤال تکمیلی بخش جاافتاده را بیرون می‌کشد."},"items":[{"answer":"In my last job we had a lot of angry customers, but our team was very good at calming them down.","present":["Situation"],"fix":{"en":"No action by the speaker and no result. Ask: \"What exactly did you do?\"","tr":"Konuşanın eylemi ve sonuç yok. Sor: \"What exactly did you do?\"","fa":"گوینده نه از کار خودش می‌گوید و نه از نتیجه. بپرس: «⁨What exactly did you do?⁩»"}},{"answer":"A client was unhappy with a late shipment. I had to keep the account. I called him the same day, explained the delay and offered free express delivery. He renewed his contract a month later.","present":["Situation","Task","Action","Result"],"fix":null},{"answer":"Our system crashed during payroll week, so I stayed late and checked every salary by hand.","present":["Situation","Action"],"fix":{"en":"Good action, but no result. Ask: \"What was the outcome?\"","tr":"Eylem iyi ama sonuç yok. Sor: \"What was the outcome?\"","fa":"کارش خوب است، اما نتیجه را نگفته. بپرس: «⁨What was the outcome?⁩»"}},{"answer":"I always stay calm under pressure. I am a very organised person.","present":[],"fix":{"en":"No real event at all: these are claims about yourself. Ask: \"Tell me about one time when that helped you.\"","tr":"Hiç gerçek olay yok: bunlar kişinin kendisi hakkındaki iddiaları. Sor: \"Tell me about one time when that helped you.\"","fa":"اصلاً اتفاق واقعی‌ای تعریف نشده؛ این‌ها فقط ادعا درباره‌ی خود است. بپرس: «⁨Tell me about one time when that helped you.⁩»"}}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-w","title":{"en":"Notes on Deniz's answer","tr":"Deniz'in cevabı için notlar","fa":"یادداشت‌ها درباره‌ی جواب دنیز"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write Leyla's interview notes on Deniz's second answer (the truck story) for Omar. Facts only: situation, his actions, the result, and one line of evaluation.","tr":"Leyla'nın, Deniz'in ikinci cevabıyla (kamyon hikâyesi) ilgili Omar için yazdığı mülakat notlarını yaz. Sadece gerçekler: durum, yaptıkları, sonuç ve tek satır değerlendirme.","fa":"یادداشت مصاحبه‌ی لیلا درباره‌ی جواب دوم دنیز (ماجرای کامیون) را برای عمر بنویس. فقط واقعیت‌ها: موقعیت، کارهایی که دنیز کرد، نتیجه و یک خط ارزیابی."},"model":"Q2 (deadline problem). Situation: March, truck broke down with medicine for 3 hospitals; manager away. Actions: he called 2 drivers, had boxes repacked into a van, phoned each hospital with a new time. Result: 2 of 3 on time, 1 four hours late; client kept. Evaluation: clear evidence of ownership and calm problem-solving under pressure.","frame":"Q2 (deadline problem). Situation: ___. Actions: he ___, he ___ and he ___. Result: ___. Evaluation: clear evidence of ___.","words":[{"word":"evidence"},{"word":"outcome"},{"word":"under pressure"}],"minWords":45,"minSentences":4,"rubric":["Task done: S, A, R and evaluation all present","Organised: one label per part","Language: past simple for actions; no opinions in the fact lines","Tone: neutral and fair, no judgement words like \"lazy\" or \"amazing\""],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: S, A, R ve değerlendirme, hepsi var","Düzen: her parçaya bir başlık","Dil: eylemler için past simple; bilgi satırlarında yorum yok","Üslup: tarafsız ve adil; \"lazy\" ya da \"amazing\" gibi yargı sözleri yok"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: S، A، R و ارزیابی، همه آمده‌اند","نظم: برای هر بخش یک عنوان","زبان: گذشته‌ی ساده برای کارها؛ در سطرهای واقعیت، نظر شخصی نیاید","لحن: بی‌طرف و منصف؛ بدون کلمه‌های قضاوتی مثل «lazy» یا «amazing»"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"The situation","tr":"Durum","fa":"موقعیت"},"find":["situation","broke down"],"sample":"March: truck broke down with medicine for 3 hospitals"},{"t":{"en":"His actions","tr":"Yaptıkları","fa":"کارهایی که کرد"},"find":["actions","he called","phoned"],"sample":"called 2 drivers, repacked into a van, phoned each hospital"},{"t":{"en":"The result","tr":"Sonuç","fa":"نتیجه"},"find":["result","on time","outcome"],"sample":"2 of 3 on time, 1 four hours late; client kept"},{"t":{"en":"One line of evaluation","tr":"Tek satırlık değerlendirme","fa":"یک خط ارزیابی"},"find":["evaluation","evidence of"],"sample":"evidence of ownership; calm under pressure"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-p","title":{"en":"Deniz on the bus home","tr":"Eve dönen otobüste Deniz","fa":"دنیز در اتوبوس برگشت به خانه"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Deniz on the bus home. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: what are you worried about, and what do you wish you had said?","tr":"Eve giden otobüsteki Deniz'sin. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: neden endişelisin ve keşke ne söyleseydim diyorsun?","fa":"تو دنیز هستی و با اتوبوس به خانه برمی‌گردی. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: نگران چه هستی و ای کاش چه چیزی را گفته بودی؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-3-2-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-3-2","type":"exit","note":"Developer note, not shown: own items = blank, blank2, one STAR item; spaced from 3.1, 2.3, 1.2.","items":[{"from":"hr-3-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Tell me about a time when you ___ a deadline.","options":["miss","missed","are missing"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"missed: 'a time when' points to one finished event, so past simple. 'Miss' is the present, and 'are missing' is happening now.","tr":"missed: 'a time when' bitmiş tek bir olayı gösterir, bu yüzden past simple. 'Miss' şimdiki zamandır; 'are missing' şu anda olandır.","fa":"missed درست است، چون a time when به یک اتفاق تمام‌شده اشاره دارد و گذشته‌ی ساده می‌خواهد. miss زمان حال است و are missing یعنی همین الان."}},{"from":"hr-3-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Could you tell me ___ the job?","options":["why you chose","why did you choose","why chose you"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"why you chose: inside 'Could you tell me...', use statement order and no did. 'Why did you choose' is question order, and 'why chose you' swaps subject and verb.","tr":"why you chose: 'Could you tell me...' içinde düz sıra kullanılır, did gelmez. 'Why did you choose' soru sırasıdır; 'why chose you' özne ile fiilin yerini değiştirir.","fa":"why you chose درست است، چون بعد از Could you tell me ترتیب خبری می‌آید و did لازم نیست. why did you choose ترتیب سؤالی است و why chose you جای فاعل و فعل را عوض می‌کند."}},{"from":"hr-3-2","kind":"mcq","prompt":"An answer has a situation and an action, but no result. Which follow-up do you ask?","options":["What was the outcome?","Could you spell that?","Where do you live now?"],"correct":0,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'What was the outcome?' asks for the missing result. Spelling and where they live have nothing to do with the answer.","tr":"'What was the outcome?' eksik sonucu sorar. Heceleme ve nerede yaşadıkları cevapla ilgili değildir.","fa":"«What was the outcome?» نتیجه‌ای را که جا افتاده می‌پرسد. هجی کردن و محل زندگی ربطی به این جواب ندارند."}},{"from":"hr-3-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"We ___ meeting the Dubai team on Thursday.","options":["are","will","going"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"are: a fixed arrangement uses are + -ing (we are meeting). 'Will meeting' and 'going meeting' are not English.","tr":"are: kesinleşmiş bir düzenleme are + -ing kullanır (we are meeting). 'Will meeting' ve 'going meeting' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"are درست است، چون قرار قطعی با are و فعل ing‌دار می‌آید (we are meeting). will meeting و going meeting انگلیسی نیستند."}},{"from":"hr-2-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Could you tell me ___ you have the right to work in the UAE?","options":["do","if","what"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"if: it opens an indirect yes/no question. 'Do' can't sit inside the sentence, and 'what' needs a missing thing.","tr":"if: dolaylı bir evet/hayır sorusu açar. 'Do' cümlenin içinde yer alamaz; 'what' eksik bir şey ister.","fa":"if درست است، چون سؤال بله‌یا‌نهِ غیرمستقیم را باز می‌کند. do داخل جمله جایی ندارد و what دنبال چیزی است که جمله ندارد."}},{"from":"hr-1-2","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which line is a polite request in an email?","options":["Send the CVs.","I was wondering if you could send the CVs.","You will send the CVs."],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"'I was wondering if you could send the CVs' is soft and polite. 'Send the CVs' is an order, and 'You will send' sounds like a command.","tr":"'I was wondering if you could send the CVs' yumuşak ve kibardır. 'Send the CVs' bir emirdir; 'You will send' buyruk gibi duyulur.","fa":"«I was wondering if you could send the CVs» نرم و مؤدبانه است. «Send the CVs» دستور است و «You will send» شبیه فرمان است."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
